<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_figure_panel">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Notes.</span><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> M1 = perceived sensitivity, M2 = perceived control, M3 = perceived usefulness. IA = Autonomy (0 = No autonomy, 1 = Intermediate autonomy). Full autonomy (IA = 2) is omitted here because it showed no significant effects in the mixed-effects models; complete IA = 2 estimates are reported in </span><a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Full Table for the Moderated Mediation Analysis Results ‣ Autonomy Matters: A Study on Personalization-Privacy Dilemma in LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix F</span></a><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>. </span><span id="S6.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effects of Intermediate Autonomy (IA, W) on mediators (M1–M3), outcomes (<math id="S6.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>: privacy concern, <math id="S6.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: trust, <math id="S6.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>: willingness to use), and indirect paths (<math id="S6.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\to M\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\to M\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>).
All coefficients are unstandardized, with 95% confidence intervals in brackets. Significant effects are shown in bold.</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
